            <ArticleTitle>Evaluation of long-term survival after successful percutaneous coronary intervention among patients with chronic renal failure.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>630-3, A9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We studied the long-term outcomes after percutaneous coronary intervention in dialysis patients and in patients with chronic renal failure (CRF) (serum creatinine &gt; or = 3.0 mg/dl). All-cause mortality at 1 year was 2.9% for the control group, 16.2% for the group with CRF, and 14.1% for dialysis patients. Cardiac mortality at 1 year was 1.9% for ther control group, 15.2% for the group with CRF, and 10.0% for dialysis patients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
